# BBG house safety rules: topic, who, rule, source
HOUSE = [
 ("Who decides", "Everyone", "Cody, the head coach at every class, decides what's taught, who spars and who's matched with whom. These plans and drills are starting points.", "BBG rule (Cody, Oct 20, 2026)"),
 ("Head contact for kids", "Under 12", "No strikes to the head in class. Kids boxing is pads, bags, footwork and games; partner work is glove taps or cooperative drilling. (Boxing Canada lets coach-led conditioned sparring start gradually from about age 9-12; Cody decides if and when, with a certified coach.)", "BBG starting rule (Cody to confirm); Boxing Canada LTAD"),
 ("Sparring", "Everyone", "Sparring with head contact only in the Competition Class, with Cody's OK, full gear (headgear, mouthguard, gloves) and a coach watching. MMA: no head or face strikes for anyone under 19 (Ontario youth MMA rules, ages 12-18).", "BBG starting rule; Ontario amateur MMA rules"),
 ("Wrestling and grappling holds", "Kids and youth", "Never: slams, back-bending throws, full or three-quarter nelsons, both hands on the neck, neck cranks, heel hooks. Throws only once breakfalls are solid. Youth submissions follow Ontario's no-gi table: straight armbar from 7, kimura from 9, rear naked choke and triangle from 11, the rest from 16.", "Ontario amateur wrestling and grappling rules (2025)"),
 ("After a hit to the head", "Everyone", "Any sign of a concussion (headache, dizzy, confused, sick, unsteady): remove them from training right away and don't let them back in that day. Tell a parent for anyone under 18 and tell Cody. Only a doctor or nurse practitioner can clear them to return, and they follow the return-to-sport steps.", "Ontario Rowan's Law"),
 ("Designated person", "Every class", "One named person at every class can remove an athlete with a suspected concussion. They've reviewed the concussion awareness resource in the last 12 months (Making Headway recommended). They don't diagnose. At BBG it's Cody for every class (Oct 2026).", "Ontario Rowan's Law; Coaches Association of Ontario; Cody"),
 ("Registration and coaches (Rowan's Law)", "Under 26", "Before registering, athletes under 26 and parents of under-18s confirm they've read Ontario's concussion awareness resource (within 12 months) and the Concussion Code of Conduct. Coaches confirm both every year. BBG has this in place (Cody, Oct 2026).", "Ontario Rowan's Law"),
 ("Coach screening", "Coaches", "Every BBG coach has a vulnerable sector check; some hold NCCP certification (Cody, Oct 2026). New coaches and helpers get a vulnerable sector check before they work with anyone under 18.", "Cody; Coaching Association of Canada, Responsible Coaching Movement"),
 ("Rule of Two", "Kids and youth", "Two screened adults present (a coach plus another coach, staff or parent). No coach alone one-on-one with a child, out of sight. No private messages to minors: group messages that include parents.", "Coaching Association of Canada, Responsible Coaching Movement"),
 ("Ages 4-5", "Youngest kids", "Cody takes kids from about 4. Keep it short and playful: footwork games, stance, punching pads a coach holds, the bag, relay races. No partner contact and no live games, a second adult present, water and rest often.", "Cody; Sport for Life, Active Start stage (ages 0-6: learn movement through active play)"),
 ("Mixed-age classes", "All-ages classes", "In an all-ages class (Boxing, Mon and Wed), split into age groups for any drill above the youngest age: younger kids do footwork, pads a coach holds, the bag or a game while older athletes partner up. Never pair a child with a teen or adult for partner or touch drills.", "BBG starting rule"),
 ("Equipment", "Coaches", "BBG has heavy bags, focus mitts, Thai pads and kick shields, wrestling mats, gloves to lend, headgear, agility ladders and cones, medicine balls and battle ropes (Cody, Oct 2026). No ring, cage or skipping ropes. Plans only use this gear.", "Cody"),
 ("Warm-up", "Everyone", "Every class starts with a 10-15 minute warm-up that builds from easy jogging to balance, landing and quick footwork. Water breaks in every class.", "BJSM 2024 review of youth injury-prevention warm-ups"),
 ("Injuries and health", "Everyone", "Coaches don't give medical advice and nobody writes health details in any sheet. Injuries go to Cody the same day.", "BBG starting rule"),
 ("Matching partners and the tap", "Everyone", "Match by size, age and experience; a coach watches every pair in live rounds and stops anything unsafe. Tap early, let go at once: practise the tap with every beginner before any live grappling.", "BBG starting rule"),
]
